sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch05-20> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Constraints on 3×3 blocks of cells can be constructed to force complex patterns: a set of 56 allowed templates forces a unique, largely random pattern equivalent to the evolution of the rule 30 cellular automaton.";
    dc:type "mathematical";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "3x3 template constraints can force a rule 30–like random pattern";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Stephen Wolfram, A New Kind of Science (Champaign, IL: Wolfram Media, 2002), Chapter 5, “Two Dimensions and Beyond”; section “Systems Based on Constraints” (from p. 210), p. 220. Scope: two-dimensional constraints on 3×3 neighborhoods"
}
